    "durationMs": 136230,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and verified end-to-end. All 13 tests pass, and I exercised every endpoint live via `sh start.sh`, including a restart to confirm clicks and links persist in MySQL.\n\nWhat I built:\n- **Migration + `Link` model** (`url` text, `code` unique varchar(20), `clicks` default 0) using the configured `DB_*` environment connection — no hard-coded credentials.\n- **`LinkController`** with POST `/links` (201, generated 8-char alphanumeric code when omitted, 409 on duplicate custom code, exact URL stored and returned unchanged), GET `/links` (ascending by id, `{\"items\", \"total\"}`), GET `/links/{code}` (200/404), GET `/r/{code}` (302 with exact `Location`, atomic `increment('clicks')` for exactly-once counting, 404).\n- **Validation**: `url:http,https` (enforces absolute http/https with host per the framework's pattern) and `code` as 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`; malformed JSON decodes to an empty payload and fails as 422. All error responses carry an `error` field.\n- **Bootstrap changes**: `api: routes/api.php` with `apiPrefix: ''` so paths are `/links` and `/r/{code}`, plus always-JSON exception rendering with a custom 422 shape.\n- **`start.sh`** (executable): applies migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` with `php artisan serve --no-reload` — verified it passes the shell's `DB_*` variables through to the server.\n- **README** section covering how to start the server plus an endpoint reference.\n\nPint is clean, the live-server smoke test passed on every requirement, and I stopped the test server and cleared my smoke-test rows so the database is clean for the real suite."
  }
